  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The masses and radii of the earth and the moon are <math><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math>, <math><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>, <math><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> respectively. Their centres are at a distance d apart. What should be the minimum speed with which a body of mass m should be projected from a point midway between their centres, so as to escape to infinity?</p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
